; E168 Phase 12, G6(i) -- MUST NOT COMPILE.
;
; THE ELEMENT'S CENTRAL CLAIM, as a refusal a built checker makes. `ex-check`
; and `gate-verdict` are `->` defs that hold no `Builder` binder, so a judgment
; body cannot reach the evidence-producing seam WITH NO CAP IN HAND: the call is
; `load: type mismatch`, not a convention anyone has to remember.
;
; ⚑ Qualified deliberately. This does NOT say a `->` def cannot reach a
; crossing -- measured, it can: a `->` def that mints its own `(builder …)` and
; calls `observe` compiles, runs, and performs the crossing. What is pinned here
; is that reaching it costs a VISIBLE LINE inside the judgment body instead of
; no line at all. Detection, not prevention; prevention is E171's or E80's.
;
; The compiling twin is e168_cap_thread.chiral. A trivial entry is present so the
; ONLY error is the load error and not "no such def: compile-main".
;
; want: exit 1, `load: type mismatch`

(import "evidence/test-floor")

(def judge (-> Str I64)
  (lam (path)
    (case (observe path)
      ((ob-nofile p b)  1)
      ((ob-nobuild w b) 2)
      ((ob-nomatch p b) 3)
      ((ob-ok o b)      0))))

(def compile-main (-> I64 I64) (lam (n) 0))
